| units: 100 tech: scmos
| generated by gen_irsim_sim.py from src/tr_1um_i2c_slave_async.extracted (whole-chip, LVS-clean)
| node names: KLayout's anonymous "$N" nets are rewritten "NN"
| (IRSIM 9.7's command interpreter treats a leading "$" as a
| variable-substitution sigil, not a plain identifier character).
| The chip's VDD/GND supply nodes (N1/VSS pre-rename)
| are renamed literally "Vdd"/"Gnd" -- IRSIM looks for those exact
| names by default and segfaulted on a real run when they weren't
| found (confirmed; see design_notes.md 76.8).
|type  gate            source          drain           length  width
| last device below (Gnd-gated PMOS, Vdd->SDA pad) is a synthetic
| weak pull-up -- see comment in gen_irsim_sim.py's main(). Not part
| of the real extracted netlist: this die's SDA driver is open-drain
| only (OSS_ESD_5V_DIO's OUT tied to Gnd; sda_oe=1 pulls SDA low,
| sda_oe=0 releases) and has no on-die pull-up device, so an external
| one is added here so the bus idles high like a real I2C bus.
